%% ChronoPlayer — watermark replay split: hot side pulled on demand from the story's keeper roster, cold side from the archive, cut at B = min(hot_floor)
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant V as ChronoVisor
  participant K as ChronoKeeper roster (story_range_fetch + legacy chunk source)
  box rgb(235,242,250) ChronoPlayer process
    participant AS as PlayerStoreAdminService
    participant DS as PlayerDataStore (roster + legacy-mirror pipeline)
    participant PS as PlaybackService
    participant HFC as KeeperHotFetchClient (per keeper, lazy + cached)
    participant QRA as QueryResponseAgent (drain ULT)
    participant RRQ as ArchiveReadingRequestQueue
    participant RA as ArchiveReadingAgent (reading ULT)
    participant HDF as HDF5ArchiveReadingAgent
  end
  actor C as Client (query requester)

  Note over V,DS: 1) ACQUIRE (roster) — the visor delivers the story's keeper roster so the player can hot-fetch at replay time
  V->>AS: start_story_recording_with_keepers(chronicle, story, story_id, t0, keeper recording ServiceIds)   [RPC]
  AS->>DS: setStoryKeepers(story_id, keeper_services)  (replaced wholesale each story start)
  AS->>DS: startStoryRecording(...)  (opens the legacy-mirror pipeline)
  AS-->>V: CL_SUCCESS

  Note over K,DS: 2) LEGACY MIRROR (optional config) — the player still receives pushed chunks over RDMA, but replay no longer reads this in-memory window
  K->>DS: receive_story_chunk(bulk, reporter)   [RDMA] -> ingest -> collect / decay -> delete (archive already holds them)

  Note over DS,HDF: 3) REPLAY QUERY (watermark split) — hot from the keeper roster on demand, cold from the archive, cut at B = min(hot_floor)
  C->>PS: story_playback_request(receiver, query_id, story_id, chronicle, story, start, end)   [RPC]
  PS->>DS: getStoryKeepers(story_id)
  DS-->>PS: keeper roster
  loop each keeper in the roster (hot fetch, fan-out)
    PS->>HFC: getHotFetchClient(keeper)  (lazy, cached by endpoint)
    PS->>HFC: fetchRange(story_id, start, end, maxEvents)
    HFC->>K: story_range_fetch(story_id, start, end, maxEvents)   [RPC]
    K-->>HFC: HotRangeResponse(events in range, hot_floor, known_W)
    HFC-->>PS: response
    PS->>PS: hot_boundary = min(hot_boundary, hot_floor), merge events (dedup by EventSequence)
    Note right of PS: unreachable / empty keeper reports hot_floor = UINT64_MAX and drops out of the min, so B only rises (archive covers the rest)
  end
  PS->>PS: B = hot_boundary, keep hot events with time ≥ B (drop < B — archive-covered by E ≤ W)
  PS->>QRA: stashQueryResponseRecord(query_id, hot response, complete = (B ≤ start))
  PS-->>C: query_id (accepted)
  opt archive portion needed (B > start)
    PS->>RRQ: pushReadingRequest(ArchiveReadingRequest chronicle, story, start, B)
  end

  Note over RA,HDF: 4) ARCHIVE READ (cold) — separate reading ULT, cut at [start, B)
  loop archiveReadingTask
    RA->>RRQ: popReadingRequest()
    RA->>HDF: readArchivedStory(chronicle, story, start, B)
    HDF-->>RA: list of StoryChunk*
    RA->>QRA: addArchivedEventsToQueryResponse(query_id, chunks)
    QRA->>QRA: prepend archived events, mark response ready
  end

  Note over QRA,C: 5) DELIVER — QueryResponseAgent drains ready responses to the client
  loop drainQueryResponses
    QRA->>C: receive_query_response(serialized bulk)   [RDMA]
    C-->>QRA: bytes_transferred
    QRA->>QRA: delete response
  end

  Note over V,DS: 6) STOP — the visor closes the story, pipeline retirement is deferred
  V->>AS: stop_story_recording(story_id)   [RPC]
  AS->>DS: stopStoryRecording(story_id)  (schedule pipeline exit at now + inactive_pipeline_delay)
  AS-->>V: CL_SUCCESS
